cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Loomground: a declarative language for the governance of AI systems and AI agents"
message: "If you use Loomground, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: flxk1
repository-code: "https://github.com/flxk1/loomground"
abstract: >
  Loomground is a Pure-Data-style declarative language for expressing governance
  constraints on AI systems and AI agents. A governance program is a patch of
  typed nodes wired by typed cords, evaluated from a single activation source,
  resolved at one master before any action takes effect, and recorded such that
  later alteration is detectable. The evaluation of the patch is the control.
keywords:
  - AI governance
  - declarative language
  - human oversight
  - provenance
  - capability security
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
# The specification (spec/) is CC-BY-4.0 (LICENSE-SPEC);
# the conformance vectors and examples are Apache-2.0 (LICENSE-CODE).
version: 0.6.0
date-released: 2026-06-27
